    "curated_prompt": "retry_if_exception_message has inverted regex-match behavior\n\nA regex-matching exception message should cause a retry. A message that does not match should propagate without retrying. The behavior is currently reversed.\n\nThis reproduction limits each call to two attempts:\n\n```python\nfrom tenacity import retry, retry_if_exception_message, stop_after_attempt, wait_none, RetryError\n\n@retry(retry=retry_if_exception_message(match=r\"retry me\"),\n       stop=stop_after_attempt(2), wait=wait_none())\ndef matching_message():\n    raise ValueError(\"retry me\")\n\n@retry(retry=retry_if_exception_message(match=r\"don't retry\"),\n       stop=stop_after_attempt(2), wait=wait_none())\ndef nonmatching_message():\n    raise ValueError(\"retry me\")\n\nfor function in (matching_message, nonmatching_message):\n    try:\n        function()\n    except RetryError:\n        print(function.__name__, \"exhausted its retry attempts\")\n    except ValueError:\n        print(function.__name__, \"propagated the exception without retrying\")\n```\n\nExpected: `matching_message` exhausts its two retry attempts; `nonmatching_message` propagates its ValueError after its first attempt. The current behavior produces the opposite outcomes.\n",
